    "excerpt": "ESP32 Marauder A suite of WiFi/Bluetooth offensive and defensive tools for the ESP32 Getting Started Download the latest release of the firmware. Check out the project wiki for a full overview of the ESP32 Marauder FCC module identifiers The Device Info screen reports the FCC ID of the radio module fitted to supported JustCallMeKoko hardware. This is the module identifier, not a claim that every carrier-board or enclosure configuration has a separate end-product grant. Hardware Radio module FCC ID --- --- --- Marauder v8, Marauder Mini v3, C5 Wardriver, C5 LowKey, BFFB v2 ESP32-C5-WROOM-U `2AC7Z-ESPC5WROOMU` Marauder v4, v6, v6.1, v7, original Mini, Marauder Kit ESP32-WROOM-32U `2AC7Z-ESP32WROOM32U` BFFB / Marauder Dev Board Pro ESP32-WROOM-32E `2AC7Z-ESP32WROOM32E` The legacy mappings are the closest modular approvals for the modules specified by the repository hardware designs. Confirm the module marking on a physical unit before using an FCC ID for labeling or compliance documentation. Third-party targets display `See hardware label` because their module or complete-device certification can vary by production revision. For Sale Now You can buy the ESP32 Marauder using this link",
